#heading(level: 1, numbering: none)[Notation] <front:notation>

$ZZ$: Integers

$QQ$: Rational numbers

$RR$: Real numbers

$CC$: Complex numbers

$FF_q$: Field of $q$ elements, of characteristic $p$.

$ZZ_ell, QQ_ell$: $ell$-adic integers, $ell$-adic numbers

If $k$ is a field, $overline(k)$ is its algebraic closure

If $X$ is a subset of a group $H$ and $g in H$, $X^g = g^(-1) X g$ and
$""^g X = g X g^(-1)$.

Let $H$ be a finite group. $abs(H)_p$ is the $p$-part of $abs(H)$, and
$abs(H)_(p')$ is the part of $abs(H)$ prime to $p$.

$cal(R)(H)$ is the Grothendieck group of $H$.

If $L$ is a subgroup of $H$ and $rho$ is a representation of $L$,
$Ind_L^(H)(rho)$ is the representation of $H$ induced by $rho$.
